---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use | PaydayCal"
  description="Terms of use for PaydayCal: free informational payday calendars, no financial advice, standard disclaimers."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose" style="padding-block: 2rem;">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: July 3, 2026</em></p>

      <h2>What PaydayCal is</h2>
      <p>
        PaydayCal provides free, informational calculators and articles about pay schedules, payday calendars, and
        related personal-finance topics. By using the site you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Not financial, tax, or legal advice</h2>
      <p>
        Content on PaydayCal is general information, not advice for your specific situation. Actual pay dates are set
        by your employer and payroll provider and can differ from the standard conventions we display (for example,
        around holidays). Always confirm dates and amounts against your own pay stub, and consult a qualified
        professional for financial, tax, or legal decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided "as is." We work hard to keep the math correct and the content current, but we make no
        warranty that the site is error-free and accept no liability for decisions made based on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You may link to, share, and print PaydayCal's output for personal use. You may not scrape, republish, or resell
        the site's content or present it as your own.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        PaydayCal displays ads served by third parties (Google AdSense). Advertisers are responsible for their own
        content; an ad's presence is not our endorsement. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how
        advertising cookies work.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms; continued use after changes means you accept them.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
